\"s90\"],\"demand\":\"current_prefs\",\"type\":\"text\",\"scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\"},\"value_ref\":\"t1\"},\"creative_changes\":{\"version\":1,\"source_ids\":[\"s24\",\"s3\",\"s25\",\"s48\",\"s4\",\"s83\",\"s82\",\"s5\",\"s50\",\"s49\",\"s23\",\"s89\",\"s26\"],\"demand\":\"creative_changes\",\"type\":\"text\",\"scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\"},\"value_ref\":\"t2\"}},\"known_observations\":[{\"id\":\"fact_aefd4bcd8a794c4b3dbe8ccb\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"source_ids\":[\"s24\",\"s34\",\"s33\",\"s42\",\"s3\",\"s41\",\"s25\",\"s4\",\"s5\",\"s14\",\"s23\",\"s15\",\"s32\",\"s13\",\"s26\",\"s16\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\",\"parent_versions\":{},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user describes both positive and negative collaborative experiences across multiple conversations. Positive experiences include blending traditional Pacific sounds with modern beats (s23-s26) and joining a local band fusing traditional and contemporary styles (s32-s34). Negative experiences include a chaotic 2019 jam session (s13-s16), feeling stifled by artistic disagreements in a band (s4-s5), and feeling intimidated in a music theory discussion group (s41-s42). These are all supported by the user's own statements in the provided source spans.\",\"variable\":\"collab_experience\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\",\"value_ref\":\"t0\"},{\"id\":\"fact_28b79de9a226b64f7e2f545a\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"source_ids\":[\"s24\",\"s3\",\"s25\",\"s48\",\"s4\",\"s92\",\"s83\",\"s82\",\"s5\",\"s50\",\"s93\",\"s49\",\"s23\",\"s89\",\"s91\",\"s26\",\"s90\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\",\"parent_versions\":{},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user describes enjoying blending traditional Pacific sounds with modern beats (s3, s23-s26), incorporating nature sounds (s48-s50), and finding joy in creating their own tracks (s91-s93). They express frustration with collaborations where artistic visions clash (s4-s5, original question), dislike for technical music theory and production (s82-s83, s89-s90), and a preference for emotional connection and storytelling in music (s83, s90). The original question confirms a desire for autonomy after stifling band experiences.\",\"variable\":\"current_prefs\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\",\"value_ref\":\"t1\"},{\"id\":\"fact_a046dba8e2819400a61f59f7\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"source_ids\":[\"s24\",\"s3\",\"s25\",\"s48\",\"s4\",\"s83\",\"s82\",\"s5\",\"s50\",\"s49\",\"s23\",\"s89\",\"s26\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\",\"parent_versions\":{},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user describes leaving a band due to clashing artistic visions (s4, s5) and feeling stifled, leading to a desire for autonomy. They later collaborated on a track blending traditional Pacific sounds with modern beats (s23, s24, s25, s26), recorded nature sounds to enrich their music (s48, s49, s50), and expressed a preference for emotional connection over music theory and technical production (s82, s83, s89). These sources collectively support a significant shift toward independent, personally resonant creative work.\",\"variable\":\"creative_changes\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\",\"value_ref\":\"t2\"}],\"source_spans\":[[\"s3\",\"d1\",107,477,\"User: It was exhilarating to showcase how our traditional sounds can coexist with modern elements, creating a beautiful and harmonious blend that resonates with a wide audience. The experience of seeing people connect with the music on a deeper level was something that I had always dreamed of achieving, as it brings the rich tapestry of our cultural heritage to life. \",\"user\",[157]],[\"s4\",\"d1\",477,827,\"However, I’ve had some challenges collaborating with other musicians, primarily stemming from differing artistic visions and contrasting approaches to the creative process. Each artist brings their unique style and preferences to the table, which can sometimes create friction rather than synergy, and that has been a tough pill to swallow at times. \",\"user\",[157]],[\"s5\",\"d1\",827,1008,\"It's disheartening when a collaboration that seems so promising on paper starts to unravel due to these differences, leaving me to ponder the best way forward in my musical journey.\",\"user\",[157]],[\"s13\",\"d2\",105,471,\"User: I organized a jam session in 2019, but it ended up chaotic and unproductive. There were several musicians with varying skill levels, and while the diversity was exciting, it also led to miscommunications about what we wanted to achieve together. With different genres and playing styles clashing, it was hard to find common ground and create a cohesive sound. \",\"user\",[34,35]],[\"s14\",\"d2\",471,796,\"I remember feeling overwhelmed as I tried to harmonize our efforts, but too many ideas collided at once, leaving us frustrated. Despite the initial enthusiasm, it quickly turned into a scramble of discordant notes and missed cues.\\n\\nUser: It felt more stressful than enjoyable, so I decided to rethink collaborative meetings. \",\"user\",[34,35]],[\"s15\",\"d2\",796,1062,\"The chaotic nature of that session really took me by surprise, as I had envisioned it as a way to foster creativity and bring fresh ideas to the table. Instead, it turned into a cacophony of differing opinions and lack of direction, where not much was accomplished. \",\"user\",[34,35]],[\"s16\",\"d2\",1062,1372,\"I realized that sometimes, too many voices can drown out the clarity needed to reach a consensus or develop a meaningful project together. So now, I'm on a journey to redefine how I approach group collaborations, aiming for a more structured and fulfilling process that nurtures rather than stifles creativity.\",\"user\",[34,35]],[\"s23\",\"d3\",105,441,\"User: Yes, I collaborated with a local musician to blend traditional Pacific sounds with modern beats for a new track. Our sessions were filled with vibrant discussions about the cultural significance of the instruments we were using, such as the ukulele and various percussion instruments that are synonymous with the Pacific Islands. \",\"user\",[67,68]],[\"s24\",\"d3\",441,744,\"It was fascinating to delve into the history of each sound and explore how we could infuse contemporary rhythms that resonate with today's audiences. We spent hours experimenting in the studio, layering tracks and harmonizing melodies, aiming to strike that balance between authenticity and innovation. \",\"user\",[67,68]],[\"s25\",\"d3\",744,1104,\"The result, I believe, will not only honor our roots but also attract listeners from different backgrounds who might find something relatable in the music.\\n\\nUser: We're having such a great time experimenting with different sounds and styles. This process has opened up a world of creativity for us, where we can explore various cultural influences and genres. \",\"user\",[67,68]],[\"s26\",\"d3\",1104,1464,\"It’s fascinating how the blending of these distinct elements enables us to craft something totally unique. Each experimental session reveals new dimensions of our musical capabilities, and it feels incredibly rewarding to witness our progress. Overall, it's not just about creating music; it's about expressing our personal journeys and emotions through sound.\",\"user\",[67,68]],[\"s32\",\"d4\",105,432,\"User: Yes! I actually joined a local band that focuses on fusing traditional and contemporary styles.\\n\\nUser: It's been amazing to work alongside others who share my passion for blending different music traditions. The dynamic interactions have sparked new ideas and fueled our creativity as we explore various genres together. \",\"user\",[83,84]],[\"s33\",\"d4\",432,735,\"We've been experimenting with a mix of instruments, from traditional strumming of acoustic guitars to the pulsating rhythms produced by electronic synthesizers. It's fascinating to see how each musician brings their unique background and influences into the mix, which creates a rich tapestry of sound. \",\"user\",[83,84]],[\"s34\",\"d4\",735,856,\"This collaborative atmosphere not only enhances our musical output but also strengthens our bonds as artists and friends.\",\"user\",[83,84]],[\"s41\",\"d5\",105,425,\"User: The discussions were intense, and I felt lost in the crowd. I wanted to engage, but everyone seemed to have a deeper understanding of music theory than I did. The sheer volume of opinions and knowledge being shared left me intimidated, as if I were standing at the edge of an ocean of information, unable to swim. \",\"user\",[32]],[\"s42\",\"d5\",425,737,\"It was also challenging to keep track of so many different conversations happening at once, which made me hesitate to contribute anything meaningful. I often found myself reading the discussions late into the night, trying to absorb as much as possible, but the complexity just compounded my sense of disconnect.\",\"user\",[32]],[\"s48\",\"d6\",105,344,\"User: It was a great way to blend my love for the outdoors with my musical creativity. The sounds of nature really added depth to the track, creating a rich tapestry of auditory experiences that transported listeners to serene landscapes. \",\"user\",[81]],[\"s49\",\"d6\",344,695,\"Moments spent in the woods, by riversides, or during rainy afternoons provided the perfect backdrop for inspiration, as I captured the essence of what it feels like to be in those environments. Each recording not only served as an instrument but also as a reminder of the memories tied to those places, enriching the emotional resonance of the music. \",\"user\",[81]],[\"s50\",\"d6\",695,817,\"This blending of natural elements with melody has truly rejuvenated my passion for creating and sharing music with others.\",\"user\",[81]],[\"s82\",\"d7\",105,482,\"User: I just lost interest halfway through and felt it was taking away the joy I find in music. There was a time when the thrill of discovering new melodies brought so much happiness, but diving too deep into the technical aspects became more of a chore. It’s curious how something that once brought joy can evolve into a source of stress when we start dissecting it too much. \",\"user\",[24]],[\"s83\",\"d7\",482,767,\"I remember the initial excitement of exploring different genres, each bringing a fresh perspective, but I struggled with the framework of music theory. Ultimately, I recognized that the essence of my love for music lay in its emotional connection rather than its analytical components.\",\"user\",[24]],[\"s89\",\"d8\",105,430,\"User: I explored audio production techniques, but it just didn’t resonate with me, and I found myself tangled in technical details rather than embracing the creativity. I realized that while understanding the mechanics of sound is important, my true passion seems to lie more in experiencing music rather than dissecting it. \",\"user\",[40,41]],[\"s90\",\"d8\",430,749,\"Despite my attempts to immerse myself in the production process, I came to feel it was more of a chore and less of the rewarding experience I had initially anticipated. I think I am more drawn to the emotional aspects of music, like the storytelling elements in lyrics or the feelings evoked by melodies and harmonies. \",\"user\",[40,41]],[\"s91\",\"d8\",749,1006,\"Perhaps, I should focus my energy on areas that allow me to connect with music on a more emotional level.\\n\\nUser: It genuinely feels much better to focus on what truly inspires me, such as creating my own tracks, which bring me immense joy and satisfaction. \",\"user\",[40,41]],[\"s92\",\"d8\",1006,1339,\"This process of creation allows me to express emotions and ideas that words sometimes fail to capture, acting as an outlet for my inner thoughts and feelings. Additionally, I find that crafting my own music provides me with a sense of accomplishment and personal growth, which is invaluable in a world often filled with uncertainty. \",\"user\",[40,41]],[\"s93\",\"d8\",1339,1686,\"Music has a way of resonating with my soul, and every track I create becomes a piece of my identity and a reflection of my experiences. In contrast, when I watched a music documentary, it felt like something was missing, as it didn’t engage me in the way I had hoped, failing to evoke that same deep connection I feel when I compose my own pieces.\",\"user\",[40,41]]],\"required_parent_versions\":{\"collab_experience\":{},\"current_prefs\":{},\"creative_changes\":{},\"response\":{\"collab_experience\":1,\"current_prefs\":1,\"creative_changes\":1}},\"rules_completion_required\":false,\"supported_task_outputs\":{},\"public_output_question\":\"After several disagreements over the artistic direction, I felt stifled, which really discouraged me from that collaborative process. It was as if the creative vision I had in mind was at odds with the direction my bandmates wanted to pursue. I remember those discussions often being emotionally charged, where opinions clashed and passion ran high, but ultimately, it was clear that I couldn't contribute to something that did not resonate with my artistic essence. Feeling restricted in that environment made me question not just my contributions, but also my abilities and instincts as an artist. This inner turmoil prompted a desire for more autonomy over my own creative endeavors, leading to a pivotal decision to explore my artistry in a more personal and independent setting.\",\"public_options\":[\"I understand that initially, you enjoyed collaborating with other musicians, finding it an enriching creative experience. However, over time, your preferences evolved due to feeling stifled by disagreements over artistic direction. This led to a shift away from collaboration, as you felt constrained and questioned your artistic abilities and instincts. Your journey reflects a transition from a collaborative approach to seeking independence in order to pursue your creative endeavors in a manner that resonates with your artistic essence.\",\"You initially felt constrained by disagreements over artistic direction, feeling stifled and questioning your artistic abilities and instincts. Afterwards, you went on to enjoy collaborating with other musicians, as it was an enriching creative experience, before ultimately seeking independence to pursue your creative endeavors.\",\"At first, you questioned your artistic abilities and instincts, feeling stifled by disagreements over artistic direction in collaborations. Nevertheless, over time, you began enjoying collaboration with other musicians as an enriching creative experience, before eventually transitioning to independence to fully resonate with your true creative essence.\",\"Initially, you felt constrained by disagreements over artistic direction, which made you question your artistic abilities and instincts. However, over time, you found collaborating with other musicians to be an enriching creative experience. This led to a shift towards collaboration, as you sought creative endeavors that resonate with your artistic essence.\"],\"terminal_expression\":{\"op\":\"var\",\"id\":\"response\"},\"personal_response_selection\":true,\"phase\":\"response_selection\",\"repair_scope\":{\"failed\":[{\"variable\":\"collab_experience\",\"id\":\"*\",\"feedback\":\"duplicate JSON key: variable\",\"observation\":null,\"slot\":null},{\"variable\":\"creative_changes\",\"id\":\"*\",\"feedback\":\"duplicate JSON key: variable\",\"observation\":null,\"slot\":null},{\"variable\":\"current_prefs\",\"id\":\"*\",\"feedback\":\"duplicate JSON key: variable\",\"observation\":null,\"slot\":null},{\"variable\":\"response\",\"id\":\"*\",\"feedback\":\"duplicate JSON key: variable\",\"observation\":null,\"slot\":null}],\"attempt\":1,\"previous_response_identity\":\"b97f511b8ac31aed7af5ad1f35522e1a276ab17d6aa049fa56d18d05bf9def6b\",\"invalid_response\":\"{\\n  \\\"slots\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"variable\\\": \\\"collab_experience\\\",\\n      \\\"observations\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"id\\\": \\\"fact_aefd4bcd8a794c4b3dbe8ccb\\\",\\n          \\\"stance\\\": \\\"support\\\",\\n          \\\"value\\\": \\\"The user has had a mix of collaborative music experiences. A positive collaboration involved blending traditional Pacific sounds with modern beats alongside a local musician, which was creatively fulfilling and resulted in a track that honored cultural roots while attracting diverse listeners. Another positive experience was joining a local band that fuses traditional and contemporary styles, which sparked new ideas and strengthened bonds. However, the user also faced challenges: a 2019 jam session was chaotic and unproductive due to clashing genres and miscommunications, leading to a decision to rethink collaborative meetings. Additionally, the user felt stifled in a band due to artistic disagreements, leading to a decision to pursue more independent creative work. The user also felt intimidated in a group discussion about music theory, feeling lost and disconnected.\\\",\\n          \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"s24\\\", \\\"s34\\\", \\\"s33\\\", \\\"s42\\\", \\\"s3\\\", \\\"s41\\\", \\\"s25\\\", \\\"s4\\\", \\\"s5\\\", \\\"s14\\\", \\\"s23\\\", \\\"s15\\\", \\\"s32\\\", \\\"s13\\\", \\\"s26\\\", \\\"s16\\\"],\\n          \\\"entity_scope\\\": \\\"user\\\",\\n          \\\"time_scope\\\": \\\"past\\\",\\n          \\\"parent_versions\\\": {},\\n          \\\"retract_ids\\\": [],\\n          \\\"reason\\\": \\\"The user describes both positive and negative collaborative experiences across multiple conversations. Positive experiences include blending traditional Pacific sounds with modern beats (s23-s26) and joining a local band fusing traditional and contemporary styles (s32-s34). Negative experiences include a chaotic 2019 jam session (s13-s16), feeling stifled by artistic disagreements in a band (s4-s5), and feeling intimidated in a music theory discussion group (s41-s42). These are all supported by the user's own statements in the provided source spans.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \\\"unresolved\\\": []\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"variable\\\": \\\"current_prefs\\\",\\n      \\\"observations\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"id\\\": \\\"fact_28b79de9a226b64f7e2f545a\\\",\\n          \\\"stance\\\": \\\"support\\\",\\n          \\\"value\\\": \\\"The user values creative autonomy and emotional connection in music-making, preferring independent creation over collaboration when artistic visions clash. They enjoy blending traditional Pacific sounds with modern beats, incorporating natural field recordings, and focusing on the emotional and storytelling aspects of music rather than technical theory or production details. They find joy and fulfillment in composing their own tracks as a form of self-expression and personal growth.\\\",\\n          \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"s24\\\", \\\"s3\\\", \\\"s25\\\", \\\"s48\\\", \\\"s4\\\", \\\"s92\\\", \\\"s83\\\", \\\"s82\\\", \\\"s5\\\", \\\"s50\\\", \\\"s93\\\", \\\"s49\\\", \\\"s23\\\", \\\"s89\\\", \\\"s91\\\", \\\"s26\\\", \\\"s90\\\"],\\n          \\\"entity_scope\\\": \\\"user\\\",\\n          \\\"time_scope\\\": \\\"current\\\",\\n          \\\"parent_versions\\\": {},\\n          \\\"retract_ids\\\": [],\\n          \\\"reason\\\": \\\"The user describes enjoying blending traditional Pacific sounds with modern beats (s3, s23-s26), incorporating nature sounds (s48-s50), and finding joy in creating their own tracks (s91-s93). They express frustration with collaborations where artistic visions clash (s4-s5, original question), dislike for technical music theory and production (s82-s83, s89-s90), and a preference for emotional connection and storytelling in music (s83, s90). The original question confirms a desire for autonomy after stifling band experiences.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \\\"unresolved\\\": []\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"variable\\\": \\\"creative_changes\\\",\\n      \\\"observations\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"id\\\": \\\"fact_a046dba8e2819400a61f59f7\\\",\\n          \\\"stance\\\": \\\"support\\\",\\n          \\\"value\\\": \\\"The user decided to leave a band due to irreconcilable artistic differences and a desire for greater creative autonomy, and has since pursued independent projects blending traditional Pacific sounds with modern beats, incorporating field recordings of nature, and exploring personal emotional expression over technical analysis.\\\",\\n          \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"s24\\\", \\\"s3\\\", \\\"s25\\\", \\\"s48\\\", \\\"s4\\\", \\\"s83\\\", \\\"s82\\\", \\\"s5\\\", \\\"s50\\\", \\\"s49\\\", \\\"s23\\\", \\\"s89\\\", \\\"s26\\\"],\\n          \\\"entity_scope\\\": \\\"user\\\",\\n          \\\"time_scope\\\": \\\"past\\\",\\n          \\\"parent_versions\\\": {},\\n          \\\"retract_ids\\\": [],\\n          \\\"reason\\\": \\\"The user describes leaving a band due to clashing artistic visions (s4, s5) and feeling stifled, leading to a desire for autonomy. They later collaborated on a track blending traditional Pacific sounds with modern beats (s23, s24, s25, s26), recorded nature sounds to enrich their music (s48, s49, s50), and expressed a preference for emotional connection over music theory and technical production (s82, s83, s89). These sources collectively support a significant shift toward independent, personally resonant creative work.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \\\"unresolved\\\": []\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"variable\\\": \\\"response\\\",\\n      \\\"observations\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"id\\\": \\\"obs_response_1\\\",\\n          \\\"stance\\\": \\\"support\\\",\\n          \\\"value\\\": \\\"I understand that initially, you enjoyed collaborating with other musicians, finding it an enriching creative experience. However, over time, your preferences evolved due to feeling stifled by disagreements over artistic direction. This led to a shift away from collabor