ions clash. They enjoy blending traditional Pacific sounds with modern beats, incorporating natural field recordings, and focusing on the emotional and storytelling aspects of music rather than technical theory or production details. They find joy and fulfillment in composing their own tracks as a form of self-expression and personal growth.\",\"t2\":\"The user decided to leave a band due to irreconcilable artistic differences and a desire for greater creative autonomy, and has since pursued independent projects blending traditional Pacific sounds with modern beats, incorporating field recordings of nature, and exploring personal emotional expression over technical analysis.\"}}"
